  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{1}{6})=-0.167\\,448\u2026\u2248-0.167\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-0.167$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.167\\,4.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.167\\,4.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.167\\,4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/f6f08d799cd2d2e80494d94cc3b18a61f73227b88b25d79c926d65e161d4ce3a.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.167\\,4 \\\\  & \u22483.309\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & \u22483.309-2\\pi \u2248-2.974\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-0.167\\,4)\\cdot (-2.974\\,2)\u22480.5,\n$$\n\nrounded to $1$ decimal place.",
